core:halfling.description:
{Halfling}

Armed with sling and stone, halflings have found a harsh existence in Antagrich. Driven from their homes by the Kreegans, halflings have been scattered to the winds. These noble fighters take refuge in the earth and have an uncanny sense of luck.

{gold|Special Ability : Minimum Luck is +1. Shoots}

factory-creatures:faHalful.description:
{Halfling Grenadier}

Armed with sling and bombs, halflings have found a harsh existence in Antagrich. Driven from their homes by the Kreegans, halflings have been scattered to the winds. These noble fighters take refuge in the earth and have an uncanny sense of luck.

A rather situative shooter, can be powerful against big groups of enemies.

{gold|Special Ability : Minimum Luck is +1. Shoots. Fireball attack.}

core:rogue.description:
{Rogue}

Rogues and Bandits abound in Antagrich. If you are able to employ them in your ranks, you will be able to spy on any nearby enemies simply by right-clicking on them.

{gold|Special Ability : Spies.}

factory-creatures:bandit.description:
{Bandit}

Rogues and Bandits abound in Antagrich. If you are able to employ them in your ranks, you will be able to spy on any nearby enemies simply by right-clicking on them.

{gold|Special Abilites : Spies, First Strike. Block Retaliation}

factory-creatures:faArma.description:
{Armadillo}

Armadillos, being local to Jadame, became tamed by the scattered groups of inventors. These are quite often used as living walls, as a source of rather delicious meat or simply as pets.

Armadillos are basically meat shields, being on the weaker side of T3s. The Armadillos are weaker than Golems, but are more costly.

