factory-creatures:faAutomaton.description:
{Termotron}

These bulky machines are made with the usage of crystals of unknown origin. Though, the predescessors of the Termotrons - Mecha Knights - were made with the usage of the Heavenly Forge tech. Despite the tech level of the Forge outcasts lowered, these mechanisms still show the Forge powers.

{gold|Special Abilities : Defensive Stance (+1 defence), Non-Living, 50% magic resistance.}

factory-creatures:faBattleAutomaton.description:
{Battle Termotron}

These bulky machines are made with the usage of crystals of unknown origin. Though, the predescessors of the Termotrons - Mecha Knights - were made with the usage of the Heavenly Forge tech. Despite the tech level of the Forge outcasts lowered, these mechanisms still show the Forge powers.

{gold|Special Abilities : Defensive Stance (+2 defence), Non-Living, 60% magic resistance, 5% enemy defence reduction.}

factory-creatures:faSpider.description:
{Automaton}

Despite not being as good as Termotrons, these spider-like mechanisms are actually the main power of the Factory. Being less costly and more offensive than defensive, Automatons can form a powerstack.

{gold|Special Ability : Non-Living, 20% magic resistance}

factory-creatures:faSentinelSpider.description:
{Sentinel Automaton}

Despite not being as good as Termotrons, these spider-like mechanisms are actually the main power of the Factory. Being less costly and more offensive than defensive, Automatons can form a powerstack.

{gold|Special Ability : Non-Living, 30% magic resistance, No Retaliatiom}

factory-creatures:faWurm.description:
{Sandworm}

The origin of these creatures is unknown, but the most popular theory is that these worms were made by Warlocks long ago. Anyway, now they are native to Jadame's wastelands. No one knows how these are controlled by the Factory forces, but it is what it is. The real answer is probably some mind control tech that remained from Forge, and probably that exact tech allows them to burrow through clouds.

{gold|Special Ability : Burrows. Immune to Blind and Stone Gaze.}

factory-creatures:faOgloi.description:
{Ogloi-Khorkhoi}

The origin of these creatures is unknown, but the most popular theory is that these worms were made by Warlocks long ago. Anyway, now they are native to Jadame's wastelands. No one knows how these are controlled by the Factory forces, but it is what it is. The real answer is probably some mind control tech that remained from Forge, and probably that exact tech allows them to burrow through clouds.

